{"name":"Sweet Ariel","hex":"#e5eae3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"ariel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of mountain gazelle, native to Arabia."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Misspelling of aerial."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ariel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ariel (The Little Mermaid)","blocks":[{"text":"Ariel is a fictional character and the titular protagonist in Walt Disney Pictures' The Little Mermaid franchise, first appearing in the 1989 animated film. Voiced by Jodi Benson, Ariel is the youngest daughter of King Triton and Queen Athena of an underwater kingdom called Atlantica. She is often rebellious, and in the first film, she longs to be a part of the human world. She marries Prince Eric, whom she rescued from a shipwreck, and together they have a daughter, Melody. She is the fourth Disney Princess, the first Disney Princess to be developed during the Disney Renaissance, and the first Disney Princess since Aurora."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/Ariel_disney.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ariel_(The_Little_Mermaid)"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christie Brinkley was one of the inspirations for Ariel's design","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChristie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Stoner2008.JPG/500px-Stoner2008.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Stoner2008.JPG/1280px-Stoner2008.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Stoner2008.JPG/500px-Stoner2008.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"For the 1989 film, many of Ariel's mannerisms were copied from Sherri Stoner's live-action performance as the character[19]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStoner2008.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Ariel-SierraBoggess.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Ariel-SierraBoggess.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut